# xgcc.pins - the aarch64 cross compiler xgcc.sh unpacks (PAD-1295), pinned by SHA-256.
#
# One line per package: sha256 size path-under-the-snapshot. The snapshot is the one the
# PAD Runtime image is built from (tools/runtime/Dockerfile, SNAPSHOT=20260801T000000Z), and
# each version is the runtime's own: binutils 2.42-4ubuntu2.10 and gcc 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1
# are what its arm-linux-gnueabihf toolchain and its native gcc are, so every library these
# programs load (binutils-common, libisl23, libmpc3, libmpfr6, libzstd1 ...) is already in
# the runtime at the exact version they were built against. glibc 2.39 is the cards' own
# (spike3 rootfs, measured). Only what a -nostdlib shared object needs: no sanitizers, no
# libgomp/libatomic/libgcc_s (a mode or shim never links them).
#
# Changing a line changes the kit's stamp, so every machine unpacks the new set once.
snapshot https://snapshot.ubuntu.com/ubuntu/20260801T000000Z
